  "conceptual_split_decision": "Two complete mathematical seams: existential/record power-of-two shape and its exact equation projection; dependent finite-address-to-bit function type. Preserve whole M/L parameters and original level equations, without inventing the bridge suggested by the filename.",
  "premise_review": [
    "All1007B original and2601B organized payloads read separately. IsPowerTwoSquare requires some k with both M.m and M.n equal2^k. BinaryCubeLevel keeps arbitrary M,level:Nat,rows_eq and cols_eq exactly.",
    "binaryCubeLevel_shape retains full M/L and exact pair of stored equations. Nothing asserts that any arbitrary matrix is square, a power of two, or equipped with a level. level0 remains valid, implying dimensions1, not0.",
    "BinaryCubeSignal retains complete M/L binders and exact Cellular.CubeAddress2L.level→Carrier.Bit. The supplied CubeAddress is Fin d→Fin(2^k), so this is an indexed function type only; no definition reads M.A or maps entries to addresses.",
    "Full captured Cube1324B,Matrix6511B,Bit930B and Basic332B providers read. Their finite function/Bit types are not replaced by the distinct global Bool BitMatrix representation. Only a complete same-source level-data companion is newly imported; original historical bindings remain unreplayed."
